  "name": "CYSTEINE QUANTITATIVE URINE",
  "code": "1072",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"125\" data-end=\"304\">The <strong data-start=\"129\" data-end=\"165\">Cysteine Quantitative Urine Test</strong> measures the amount of <strong data-start=\"189\" data-end=\"201\">cysteine</strong>, a sulfur-containing amino acid, excreted in the urine over a 24-hour period. It is primarily used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"306\" data-end=\"591\">\n<li data-start=\"306\" data-end=\"420\">\n<p data-start=\"308\" data-end=\"420\"><strong data-start=\"308\" data-end=\"344\">Screen for or monitor cystinuria</strong>, a rare inherited disorder where kidneys fail to reabsorb cystine properly.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"421\" data-end=\"490\">\n<p data-start=\"423\" data-end=\"490\">Detect <strong data-start=\"430\" data-end=\"457\">cystine stone formation</strong> in the kidneys or urinary tract.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"491\" data-end=\"591\">\n<p data-start=\"493\" data-end=\"591\">Evaluate <strong data-start=\"502\" data-end=\"537\">amino acid metabolism disorders</strong>, especially in children with recurrent kidney stones.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"593\" data-end=\"724\">Cystine is poorly soluble in urine, and when its concentration exceeds solubility, it forms crystals and <strong data-start=\"698\" data-end=\"723\">cystine kidney stones</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"783\" data-end=\"850\">Elevated urinary cysteine levels are most commonly associated with:</p>\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_80l1q_1\">\n<div class=\"_tableWrapper_80l1q_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"852\" data-end=\"1392\">\n<thead data-start=\"852\" data-end=\"958\">\n<tr data-start=\"852\" data-end=\"958\">\n<th data-start=\"852\" data-end=\"875\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"854\" data-end=\"867\">Condition</strong></th>\n<th data-start=\"875\" data-end=\"958\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"877\" data-end=\"892\">Explanation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody data-start=\"1067\" data-end=\"1392\">\n<tr data-start=\"1067\" data-end=\"1174\">\n<td data-start=\"1067\" data-end=\"1091\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1069\" data-end=\"1083\">Cystinuria</strong></td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1091\" data-end=\"1174\">Inherited defect in renal tubular reabsorption of cystine and other amino acids</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1283\">\n<td data-start=\"1175\" data-end=\"1199\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1177\" data-end=\"1195\">Cystine stones</strong></td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1199\" data-end=\"1283\">Excess cystine in urine leads to precipitation and stone formation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr data-start=\"1284\" data-end=\"1392\">\n<td data-start=\"1284\" data-end=\"1308\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1286\" data-end=\"1303\">Aminoaciduria</strong></td>\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1308\" data-end=\"1392\">Generalized tubular dysfunction may cause excess excretion of amino acids</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n</div>\n<h3 data-start=\"731\" data-end=\"781\">&nbsp;</h3>",
